# User Stories

This document describes the expected behavior of the Speaking Portfolio System from the perspective of its users.

---

# Student User Stories

## Authentication

### STU-001 Login

As a student,
I want to log in using my Microsoft 365 account,
so that I do not need to create a separate username and password.

### STU-002 Automatic Access

As a student,
I want the system to recognize me automatically after login,
so that I can immediately access my classes and assignments.

---

## Assignment Management

### STU-003 View Assignments

As a student,
I want to see all assignments available to me,
so that I know what work must be completed.

### STU-004 View Assignment Details

As a student,
I want to view assignment instructions and deadlines,
so that I understand the requirements before submitting.

### STU-005 Select Assignment

As a student,
I want to select a specific assignment,
so that I can submit work for that activity.

---

## Partner Selection

### STU-006 Choose Partners

As a student,
I want to choose my speaking partners from a teacher-approved list,
so that the system knows who participated in the activity with me.

### STU-007 View Partner Information

As a student,
I want to see my selected partners,
so that I can confirm the correct people were chosen.

---

## Audio Submission

### STU-008 Upload Recording

As a student,
I want to upload my audio recording,
so that my spoken contribution can be assessed.

### STU-009 Submission Confirmation

As a student,
I want confirmation that my recording was uploaded successfully,
so that I know my work was received.

### STU-010 Replace Recording

As a student,
I want to replace my recording before the deadline,
so that I can fix mistakes or upload a better version.

---

## Transcript Review

### STU-011 Receive Transcript

As a student,
I want an AI-generated transcript of my recording,
so that I can review what was transcribed.

### STU-012 Audio and Transcript Synchronization

As a student,
I want to listen to my recording while reading the transcript,
so that I can identify transcription errors.

### STU-013 Edit Transcript

As a student,
I want to edit the transcript,
so that it accurately reflects what I said.

### STU-014 Remove Other Speakers

As a student,
I want to remove words spoken by other people,
so that only my own contribution remains.

### STU-015 Save Draft

As a student,
I want my transcript edits to be saved,
so that I do not lose my work.

---

## Metrics

### STU-016 View Statistics

As a student,
I want to see my calculated speaking statistics,
so that I understand my participation level.

### STU-017 View Word Count

As a student,
I want to see my word count,
so that I know how much I contributed.

### STU-018 View Turn Count

As a student,
I want to see my turn count,
so that I know how often I participated.

### STU-019 View Average Words Per Turn

As a student,
I want to see my average words per turn,
so that I can reflect on the quality of my participation.

---

## Submission

### STU-020 Submit Assignment

As a student,
I want to submit my final transcript,
so that it can be reviewed by my teacher.

### STU-021 View Submission Status

As a student,
I want to know whether my submission is Draft, Submitted, or Graded,
so that I understand its current status.

### STU-022 View Feedback

As a student,
I want to view my teacher's feedback,
so that I can improve future speaking performance.

---

# Teacher User Stories

## Class Management

### TCH-001 Create Class

As a teacher,
I want to create a class,
so that students can be organized into groups.

### TCH-002 Edit Class

As a teacher,
I want to update class information,
so that records remain accurate.

### TCH-003 Archive Class

As a teacher,
I want to archive completed classes,
so that active classes remain organized.

---

## Student Management

### TCH-004 Import Students

As a teacher,
I want to import students using a CSV file,
so that large classes can be created efficiently.

### TCH-005 View Student List

As a teacher,
I want to view all students in a class,
so that I can manage enrollment.

### TCH-006 Remove Students

As a teacher,
I want to remove students from a class,
so that enrollment records remain accurate.

---

## Assignment Management

### TCH-007 Create Assignment

As a teacher,
I want to create assignments,
so that students can complete speaking activities.

### TCH-008 Edit Assignment

As a teacher,
I want to update assignment settings,
so that requirements can be adjusted.

### TCH-009 Close Assignment

As a teacher,
I want to close submissions after a specific date,
so that deadlines can be enforced.

---

## Submission Review

### TCH-010 View Submissions

As a teacher,
I want to view all submissions for an assignment,
so that I can assess student work.

### TCH-011 Filter Submissions

As a teacher,
I want to filter submissions by class,
so that I can review specific groups.

### TCH-012 Open Submission

As a teacher,
I want to open a student's submission,
so that I can review their work.

### TCH-013 Listen to Audio

As a teacher,
I want to listen to student audio,
so that I can evaluate speaking performance.

### TCH-014 View Transcript

As a teacher,
I want to view the student's transcript,
so that I can assess content and participation.

### TCH-015 Compare Partners

As a teacher,
I want to see partner submissions side-by-side,
so that I can compare participation levels.

### TCH-016 View Metrics

As a teacher,
I want to see speaking statistics,
so that I can quickly identify participation patterns.

---

## Grading

### TCH-017 Enter Grade

As a teacher,
I want to assign a grade,
so that student performance can be evaluated.

### TCH-018 Provide Feedback

As a teacher,
I want to leave written comments,
so that students receive constructive feedback.

### TCH-019 Edit Grade

As a teacher,
I want to update grades when necessary,
so that corrections can be made.

---

## Reporting

### TCH-020 Export Results

As a teacher,
I want to export assignment data,
so that I can perform additional analysis.

### TCH-021 Export CSV

As a teacher,
I want to export data as CSV,
so that it can be opened in Excel.

### TCH-022 View Class Summary

As a teacher,
I want to view overall statistics for a class,
so that I can monitor participation trends.

---

## Security

### TCH-023 Restricted Access

As a teacher,
I want access only to my own classes,
so that student data remains secure.

---

# Admin User Stories

## Teacher Management

### ADM-001 Create Teacher

As an administrator,
I want to create teacher accounts,
so that instructors can access the system.

### ADM-002 Disable Teacher

As an administrator,
I want to deactivate teacher accounts,
so that only authorized staff have access.

### ADM-003 Assign Classes

As an administrator,
I want to assign classes to teachers,
so that responsibilities are clearly defined.

---

## System Management

### ADM-004 View All Classes

As an administrator,
I want to view all classes,
so that I can monitor system-wide activity.

### ADM-005 View All Assignments

As an administrator,
I want to access all assignments,
so that I can oversee usage.

### ADM-006 View All Submissions

As an administrator,
I want to review any submission,
so that support and auditing can be performed.

---

## Reporting

### ADM-007 Export Institution Data

As an administrator,
I want to export all assignment data,
so that institution-wide reporting can be produced.

### ADM-008 Export by Assignment

As an administrator,
I want to export data by assignment,
so that outcomes can be analyzed across classes.

### ADM-009 Export by Teacher

As an administrator,
I want to export data by teacher,
so that reporting can be segmented appropriately.

---

# System User Stories

## Automatic Transcript Generation

### SYS-001

As the system,
I will generate a transcript after audio upload,
so that students can review their speech.

---

## Automatic Word Count

### SYS-002

As the system,
I will calculate the total number of words in the final transcript,
so that participation metrics are available.

---

## Automatic Turn Count

### SYS-003

As the system,
I will count each line break as a speaking turn,
so that turn statistics can be generated.

---

## Automatic Average Calculation

### SYS-004

As the system,
I will calculate average words per turn,
so that participation indicators are available.

Formula:

Average Words Per Turn = Word Count / Turn Count

Rounded to two decimal places.

---

## Data Security

### SYS-005

As the system,
I will protect student and teacher data based on assigned permissions,
so that users only access authorized information.

---

# MVP Scope

The following user stories are considered essential for the first release:

- STU-001 to STU-020
- TCH-001 to TCH-021
- ADM-001 to ADM-007
- SYS-001 to SYS-005

All remaining stories may be implemented in later releases.
